## Common Workflows with Claude Code

### Workflow 1: Create Feature Branch → Commit → Create PR

```bash
# 1. Create and switch to feature branch
git checkout -b feature/new-feature

# 2. Make changes (Claude Code handles this)

# 3. Stage and commit
git add .
git commit -m "Add new feature"

# 4. Push to remote
git push -u origin feature/new-feature

# 5. Create PR
gh pr create --title "Add new feature" \
  --body "This PR adds the new feature. It includes..."
```

### Workflow 2: Review and Merge a PR

```bash
# List open PRs
gh pr list

# View PR details
gh pr view 123

# Review the PR
gh pr review 123 --approve

# Merge the PR
gh pr merge 123 --squash --delete-branch
```

### Workflow 3: Work with Multiple Reviewers

```bash
# Create PR with multiple reviewers
gh pr create --title "Important feature" \
  --body "Description" \
  --reviewer @user1,@user2,@user3

# Check review status
gh pr view 123

# Request changes from specific reviewer
gh pr review 123 --request-changes -b "Please update..."
```

### Workflow 4: Link Issues to PRs

```bash
# Create PR that closes an issue
gh pr create --title "Fix: Login bug" \
  --body "Fixes #123"

# Comment on PR with issue reference
gh pr comment 123 -b "Fixes #456"
```

